WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.335 --> 00:00:02.867
- You know, many of these meteorites

00:00:02.867 --> 00:00:05.036
are billions of years old.

00:00:05.036 --> 00:00:07.487
Imagine you holding that in your hand,

00:00:07.487 --> 00:00:10.536
the earliest part of the solar system.

00:00:10.536 --> 00:00:12.005
It feels amazing.

00:00:12.005 --> 00:00:16.146
(playful orchestral music)

00:00:16.146 --> 00:00:19.569
My name is Naveen Jain,
and I'm an entrepreneur.

00:00:19.569 --> 00:00:21.362
I started the collection
about five years ago

00:00:21.362 --> 00:00:24.155
and many people would say
that I probably do have

00:00:24.155 --> 00:00:28.322
the largest collection of
meteorites in private hands.

00:00:29.723 --> 00:00:32.543
When you look at the stuff and
people say it's just a rock

00:00:32.543 --> 00:00:35.738
until you see in the
microscope and see, oh my god,

00:00:35.738 --> 00:00:39.527
what you really have in
your hand is space gems.

00:00:39.527 --> 00:00:42.251
I am just such a curious person.

00:00:42.251 --> 00:00:45.255
So, when you're holding a
piece of moon in your hand,

00:00:45.255 --> 00:00:47.135
it's not just a piece of moon.

00:00:47.135 --> 00:00:50.819
It's really symbolic of
what we as humans are,

00:00:50.819 --> 00:00:52.510
which are explorers.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:54.012
When we get inspired, what do we do?

00:00:54.012 --> 00:00:55.201
We look up.

00:00:55.201 --> 00:00:58.246
Every star that we see is really

00:00:58.246 --> 00:01:01.439
one square inch of our own galaxy.

00:01:01.439 --> 00:01:03.297
So, when something falls on Earth,

00:01:03.297 --> 00:01:06.547
we have no idea what body it came from.

00:01:08.129 --> 00:01:09.772
This is a great meteorite.

00:01:09.772 --> 00:01:12.424
This has 20-plus amino acids,

00:01:12.424 --> 00:01:14.874
so it's quite likely these amino acids

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:17.607
became the foundation
for who we are today.

00:01:17.607 --> 00:01:19.927
So, when someone says
we're looking for aliens,

00:01:19.927 --> 00:01:21.353
all we have to do is look around us.

00:01:21.353 --> 00:01:23.777
We all could be aliens.

00:01:23.777 --> 00:01:26.142
This is a great meteorite.

00:01:26.142 --> 00:01:27.831
The whitest stuff that you see

00:01:27.831 --> 00:01:30.924
is the earliest part of our universe.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.777
And many of these things have formed

00:01:32.777 --> 00:01:35.016
at the time of the Big Bang.

00:01:35.016 --> 00:01:36.497
There's no doubt in my mind

00:01:36.497 --> 00:01:40.258
that space is going to be a next frontier.

00:01:40.258 --> 00:01:41.748
And it's a very simple reason:

00:01:41.748 --> 00:01:45.173
every single thing that we value on Earth

00:01:45.173 --> 00:01:47.478
is in abundance in space.

00:01:47.478 --> 00:01:51.094
We are just nothing but
a tiny pale blue dot.

00:01:51.094 --> 00:01:53.927
(light pop music)

